    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Sablefish, BC coast\"\nparams:\n  stock_id: \"sablefish\"\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n::: {.disclaimer}\nExploratory personal project. Not an official assessment and not a seafood recommendation.\n:::\n\n::::: {.columns}\n\n:::: {.column width=\"36%\"}\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"stock-card\">\n<div class=\"card-head\" style=\"background:#2c3e50;\">\n<div class=\"card-species\">Sablefish</div>\n<div class=\"card-title\">Sablefish, BC coast</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"badges\">\n<span class=\"badge\" style=\"background:#1a7f4b;\">DFO 2024: Healthy</span>\n<span class=\"badge tier\">Data tier A</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"stat\">2.94× LRP</div>\n<div class=\"stat-label\">Biomass relative to the limit reference point, 2021</div>\n<img class=\"spark\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Sparkline of biomass relative to the limit reference point for Sablefish, BC coast\"/>\n<dl>\n<dt>Evidence</dt>\n<dd>Biomass and fishing pressure relative to MSY</dd>\n<dt>Managed by</dt>\n<dd>Fisheries and Oceans Canada (DFO)</dd>\n<dt>Status method</dt>\n<dd>Scientific Peer Review Process</dd>\n<dt>RAM assessment period</dt>\n<dd>1962-2021</dd>\n</dl>\n<div class=\"fun\">Fun fact: Often sold as 'black cod', although it is not a true cod.</div>\n<div class=\"note\">Coastwide stock; pin position is illustrative.</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n::::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"4%\"}\n::::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](sablefish_files/figure-html/trend-1.png){width=768}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n[Download the 2-page rapid assessment (PDF)](../reports/output/rapid_assessment_sablefish.pdf){.btn .btn-primary}\n::::\n\n:::::\n\n\n## Kobe plot\n\n![](sablefish_files/figure-html/kobe-1.png){width=75%}\n\n## Management context\n\n\nText in quotation marks is copied exactly as published in DFO's 2024 Sustainability Survey for Fisheries, including any typos.\n\n- **Limit reference point, as described by DFO:** “0.4 of BMSY, where BMSY is 22,720 metric tonnes Estimated reference points in 2022 available from: https://www.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/csas-sccs/Publications/SAR-AS/2023/2023\\_010-eng.html”\n- **Upper stock reference, as described by DFO:** “0.8 of BMSY, where BMSY is 22,720 metric tonnes. Estimated reference points in 2022 available from: https://www.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/csas-sccs/Publications/SAR-AS/2023/2023\\_010-eng.html”\n- **Limit used for this project's indicator:** 0.4 x Bmsy (DFO default proxy; the 2024 survey reports this LRP for sablefish)\n- **Management plan, as reported by DFO:** “Pacific Integrated Fisheries Management Plan - GROUNDFISH - Effective Feb 21, 2024 - Feb 20, 2025 (Current Pacific Integrated Fisheries Management plan - GROUNDFISH - Effective Feb 21, 2025 - Feb 20, 2026)”\n- **Managed by:** Fisheries and Oceans Canada (DFO)\n\n\n**Science documents cited by DFO in the 2024 survey:**\n\n- <http://www.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/csas-sccs/Publications/ScR-RS/2020/2020_025-eng.html>\n- <https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/41102587.pdf>\n- <http://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/Library/344257.pdf>\n- <https://www.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/csas-sccs/Publications/ScR-RS/2024/2024_013-eng.html>\n\n## Data gaps and caveats\n\n\n- Time series ends in 2021; the DFO zone is from the 2024 survey.\n\n[← Back to all stock cards](../cards.qmd)\n\n",
